          "prompt": "Why restrict the domain of sine before inverting?",
          "workedSolution": {
            "steps": [
              "Sine repeats, so it is not one-to-one.",
              "Restricting to [−π/2, π/2] fixes that."
            ],
            "answer": "to make it one-to-one"
